# L §5.14 at e, §4.4 A movement takes a day (tally 2.3, #247; the plan's L14): an `at` that gives a window is a hole
# `at`, read as a hole `at` is: the instance and its day are the hole, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; a pin of the cell
# answers it. Before: one evaluation per law-date class, and the instance booked on its `on` (o_may 600.00 PLN).
=== m.tally
model hat
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rate: money PLN
input lw: date
input pday: date
move pay_w: transfers
  on pday
  at lw
  leg cash from world to other amount rate
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 100.00 PLN "c"
  pday = 2026-04-15 "c"
  lw = window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-10) "c"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
  opening[other] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
ask o_mar: bal(other, 2026-03-31)
ask o_may: bal(other, 2026-05-31)
ask o_pin: bal(other, 2026-05-31) with lw = 2026-02-05
ask d_w: pay_w.day
=== expect
d_w: ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-10) not precise enough for the law date of pay_w" (lw)
  unknown day: lw
  cut 2026-04-20
o_mar: ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-10) not precise enough for the law date of pay_w" (lw)
  unknown day: lw
  cut 2026-04-20
o_may: ?"date within window(2026-02-01, 2026-02-10) not precise enough for the law date of pay_w" (lw)
  unknown day: lw
  cut 2026-04-20
o_pin: 600.00 PLN
  pinned: lw = 2026-02-05
  unfulfilled: pay_w
  cut 2026-04-20
